scope: |
  SSC3-13c — the prelude's `object Dataset.of` is a VARARG WORKAROUND, written when the language
  had no varargs, and SSC3-14b landed them. It declares SIXTEEN parameters each defaulted to a
  `DsAbsent()` sentinel and then sixteen `if x != DsAbsent() then xs = xs :+ x` lines.
  (`v3/SPRINT.md` is claimed by `bench-b4-three-version-table`, now `in-progress`, so the plan is
  here — in git, before the edit — as it was for SSC3-14b and SSC3-14c.)

  THIS ONE IS EXPECTED TO CHANGE BEHAVIOUR, WHICH IS WHY IT IS WORTH DOING. The sixteen parameters
  are a HARD CAP and it is reachable — measured before claiming:

      Dataset.of(1..16)   -> works
      Dataset.of(1..17)   -> call to 'Dataset.of' passes 17 argument(s), it takes 16

  A refusal whose number comes from an implementation detail of the workaround. `T*` has no cap, so
  the seventeenth element starts working. That is the first thing varargs actually BUY: SSC3-14b
  itself moved N by zero and closed four front divergences, and the reason it bought nothing was
  precisely this workaround standing in for it.

  MEASURED BEFORE CLAIMING, so the blast radius is known rather than hoped: 47 `Dataset.of(` call
  sites in the tree, the largest passing TEN arguments, and NONE of them uses a named argument —
  `Dataset.of(a = 1, c = 3)` would be the one shape a vararg cannot express, and it does not occur.
  `collectVarargs` deliberately leaves a call with named arguments alone, so even a new one would
  keep its present behaviour rather than being silently rewrapped.

  RISK: the prelude is loaded by EVERY program, so this is the highest-leverage file in the tree to
  get wrong, and `Dataset.of` is called 47 times. The check is N with floors DIFF 3 and CRASH 9
  against the same tree minus exactly this change, plus the four `dataset-*` corpus cases read
  individually — they are the ones that exercise it, and a bucket count can hide one case moving
  from PASS to DIFF while another moves the other way.

  ALSO CHECK `DsAbsent` ITSELF. It exists only to mark an unfilled parameter; if nothing else in the
  prelude or the corpus references it, it goes with the workaround rather than being left as a type
  nobody can construct a reason for. Grep before deleting, not after.
next: replace the sixteen parameters with `items: Any*`, prove 17 works, then measure N
